defmodule <%= inspect @module %> do
  @moduledoc """
  Where every page appears in navigation.

  The sidebar and the apps grid are two renderings of this, filtered through
  `<%= inspect @access_control %>` — a group with nothing reachable in it has no
  tile and no heading, so what a user is offered is what their role actually
  unlocks.
<%= if @router do %>
  Paths are not repeated from the router: `AshQuick.Nav.Info` finds every
  QuickView by walking `<%= inspect @router %>`, and each one's label comes from
  its resource's `plural_name`. An `entry` here states only what the router
  cannot — an icon, a label the resource gets wrong, or a page that is not a
  QuickView at all. A `group` is what puts a tile in the apps grid.
<% else %>
  No router is declared, so the registry is what this module declares alone.
  Add `router: MyAppWeb.Router` to the `use` below and every QuickView becomes
  an entry without being listed here.
<% end %>  """
<%= if @router do %>
  use AshQuick.Nav, router: <%= inspect @router %>, access_control: <%= inspect @access_control %>
<% else %>
  use AshQuick.Nav, access_control: <%= inspect @access_control %>
<% end %>
  nav do
  end
end
